1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,709
Open the original call in Omni Dispatch.

2
00:00:02,889 --> 00:00:07,945
Before adding a record, check the call name and number so you attach it to the right incident.

3
00:00:08,265 --> 00:00:11,188
Open the Records tab, then select New Record.

4
00:00:11,368 --> 00:00:14,248
Starting here keeps the new record linked to this call.

5
00:00:14,568 --> 00:00:16,445
Choose Callback from the record list.

6
00:00:16,625 --> 00:00:18,716
This is the built-in system form.

7
00:00:19,036 --> 00:00:26,076
The form opens with fields for the initial report, cause, location, and the people or resources involved.

8
00:00:26,256 --> 00:00:28,517
Fill in what applies to your department.

9
00:00:28,837 --> 00:00:31,675
Enter what was first reported and the location.

10
00:00:31,855 --> 00:00:37,337
For this training example, a crew reported that the station exterior inspection was complete.

11
00:00:37,657 --> 00:00:41,305
In Narrative, explain who you called back and what you confirmed.

12
00:00:41,485 --> 00:00:44,173
Then select Save and send to store the draft.

13
00:00:44,493 --> 00:00:46,819
The draft opens with the saved details.

14
00:00:46,999 --> 00:00:49,964
Review them here, and use Save if you make a correction.

15
00:00:50,284 --> 00:00:54,337
When the record is complete, confirm the attestation and choose Finalize.

16
00:00:54,657 --> 00:00:57,943
Check the permanent Callback number on the finalized record.

17
00:00:58,263 --> 00:01:00,460
Return to the call and open Records.

18
00:01:00,640 --> 00:01:07,467
The Callback is listed with its number and Finalized status, so another dispatcher can find it from the incident.

19
00:01:07,647 --> 00:01:13,172
A search and rescue base could use the same form to document a check-back with a field team.
